# Laravel Patterns (Infrastructure & Framework Glue)

**Status:** ACTIVE — **subordinate guidance only**  
**Precedence:** Never overrides `01-ARCHITECTURE.mdc`, `clean-architecture.mdc`, or `architecture-governance.mdc`.

```text
SIS Constitution → Core Architecture → Clean Architecture / Architecture Governance
→ Module contracts → Security / Database / API → Laravel patterns (this file)
```

## Where This Rule Applies

Use these conventions **only** in permitted layers:

| Layer | Laravel patterns OK? |
|-------|----------------------|
| `app/Domain/**` | **No** — pure PHP only |
| `app/Application/**` | **No** — handlers, commands, DTOs only |
| `app/Infrastructure/**` | **Yes** — Eloquent records, repositories, jobs, listeners |
| `app/Http/**` | **Thin only** — delegate to handlers; policies OK |
| Legacy `app/Models/**` | **Migrate away** — no new business logic |

## Infrastructure Models (Eloquent Records)

- One persistence model per blueprint table in `app/Infrastructure/Persistence/` (or existing legacy `app/Models/` during migration)
- Namespace by context: e.g. `App\Infrastructure\Persistence\Students\StudentRecord`
- Always define `$casts` for dates (datetime), decimals, JSONB
- Prefer status + `effective_to` over `SoftDeletes` for academic data
- Scope queries by academic year: `scopeForAcademicYear($query, $yearId)`
- Mass assignment: `$fillable = []` on sensitive records; set fields only in repository adapters

## Relationships (Infrastructure only)

```php
public function student(): BelongsTo
public function academicYear(): BelongsTo
public function section(): BelongsTo
```

## Business Logic — NOT Service Classes

```text
❌ EnrollmentService with domain rules in app/Services/
✅ EnrollStudentHandler in app/Application/Enrollment/Commands/
✅ EnrollmentPolicy + FormRequest for HTTP concerns
```

Do **not** create conventional Laravel "Service" classes for domain workflows. Application **handlers** own use cases and transactions.

## Queue Jobs for Heavy Operations

```php
// ❌ BAD — blocks HTTP request
foreach ($students as $student) { generateCertificate($student); }

// ✅ GOOD — dispatch from handler/listener
GenerateCertificatesJob::dispatch($schoolId, $yearId)
    ->withIdempotencyKey("cert-{$schoolId}-{$yearId}");
```

## Audit (Infrastructure)

Log sensitive changes via audit infrastructure — not ad hoc in controllers:

```php
// From listener or infrastructure adapter after handler success
AuditService::log('updated', $enrollment, $oldValues, $newValues);
```

## Authorization (HTTP + Policies)

Policies scoped to school/role; controllers call `$this->authorize()` — rules live in Policy + Domain, not controller branches.

## Eager Loading (Infrastructure queries)

```php
// ❌ N+1
EnrollmentRecord::all()->each(fn ($e) => $e->student->name);

// ✅
EnrollmentRecord::with(['student', 'section', 'academicYear'])->get();
```

## When Unsure

Read `architecture-governance.mdc` and run `php artisan sis:make-feature {Context}` — do not default to Model + Controller CRUD.
